      {
        "id": 71495,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-27T03:25:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It's interesting you brought up Bunker. An ability that says you can take a card into hand is probably a legit way to gain cards while in turret mode. Draw is a pretty core term, so I could see them being different since they didnt use that word.&nbsp;</p><p>But mechanically speaking, taking the top card of your deck into hand is really the same thing as drawing a card. And in that case, should there even be a difference?</p><p>although, in a situation where you reveal the top card and decide whether to put it into your hand or replace it then take it, I think I would be hesitant to call that drawing as those were both very different effects mechanically.</p><p>With all that said, I think the safe answer Is to assume they are different (else why not just say draw for consistency sake).&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:40.423Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
